# Paths that never count as code the wiki should cover. Git pathspecs, one per line.
# A plain `*` also crosses directories here: `*.md` matches README.md and docs/a/b.md alike.
# A line starting with `!` brings paths back, whatever order it appears in: `!docs/adr/**`.
#
# This is a starting point. The first wikipoke-ingest pass tailors it to this repository:
# tests, generated files, fixtures and build plumbing usually belong here. Ignoring something is a
# conscious call; coverage keeps listing whatever is neither ignored nor documented.

# the wiki itself, documentation and agent configuration
wiki/**
.wikipoke.json
*.md
# ...but in a repository whose product is prose - prompts, skills, agent instructions, a spec -
# that Markdown IS the code, and a `!` line brings it back:
#   !prompts/**
.agents/**
.claude/**
.codex/**
.cursor/**
.opencode/**
.github/**

# lockfiles
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
bun.lockb
composer.lock
Cargo.lock
Gemfile.lock
poetry.lock
uv.lock
go.sum

# repository plumbing
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.editorconfig
.npmrc
.nvmrc
.node-version
.dockerignore

# tests and test configuration (24 *.spec.ts alongside each use case / mapper)
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.test.ts
apps/web/playwright.config.ts

